/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (Political instability and corruption are two issues that are often connected. Political instability can take the form of coups, disputed elections, election-related violence, civil conflict, or unconstitutional changes of government. Corruption can include bribery, embezzlement, nepotism, misuse of public funds, and using political power for personal benefit.)
/E (Political instability and corruption are two issues that are often connected. Political instability can take the form of coups, disputed elections, election-related violence, civil conflict, or unconstitutional changes of government. Corruption can include bribery, embezzlement, nepotism, misuse of public funds, and using political power for personal benefit.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (The effects of these issues go beyond politics. When governments are unstable or public resources are not properly managed, ordinary citizens can be affected through limited access to quality education, healthcare, infrastructure, jobs, and other essential services. Corruption can also reduce trust in government and increase inequality, while political instability can make it even harder for institutions to function effectively.)
/E (The effects of these issues go beyond politics. When governments are unstable or public resources are not properly managed, ordinary citizens can be affected through limited access to quality education, healthcare, infrastructure, jobs, and other essential services. Corruption can also reduce trust in government and increase inequality, while political instability can make it even harder for institutions to function effectively.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (The African Union has recognised the importance of tackling these challenges through initiatives such as agenda 2063 and theAfrican charter on democracy, elections and governance These frameworks focus on building peaceful, democratic, accountable, and well-governed African states. However, it is important to recognise that Africa is not facing one single political situation. Every member state has its own history and challenges, meaning that effective solutions must be realistic, sustainable, and suited to the different circumstances of African countries.)
/E (The African Union has recognised the importance of tackling these challenges through initiatives such as agenda 2063 and theAfrican charter on democracy, elections and governance These frameworks focus on building peaceful, democratic, accountable, and well-governed African states. However, it is important to recognise that Africa is not facing one single political situation. Every member state has its own history and challenges, meaning that effective solutions must be realistic, sustainable, and suited to the different circumstances of African countries.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
