/T (In the years after independence, a number of African countries experienced military coups, civil wars, authoritarian leadership, and political conflicts. The Cold War also influenced politics across the continent, with outside powers supporting different governments and political groups. These conflicts made it harder for some countries to develop strong and stable political institutions.)
/E (In the years after independence, a number of African countries experienced military coups, civil wars, authoritarian leadership, and political conflicts. The Cold War also influenced politics across the continent, with outside powers supporting different governments and political groups. These conflicts made it harder for some countries to develop strong and stable political institutions.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (At the same time, weak institutions and limited accountability created opportunities for corruption to grow. In some cases, public resources were misused, political positions were used for personal or political gain, and citizens had little power to hold leaders accountable. Although Africa has made major progress since independence, the effects of some of these historical challenges can still be seen in the political and economic situations of certain countries today.)
/E (At the same time, weak institutions and limited accountability created opportunities for corruption to grow. In some cases, public resources were misused, political positions were used for personal or political gain, and citizens had little power to hold leaders accountable. Although Africa has made major progress since independence, the effects of some of these historical challenges can still be seen in the political and economic situations of certain countries today.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
