261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 100 0 R
/T (Africa is currently facing serious challenges with political instability and corruption, which continue to deeply affect the socio-economic development and overall peace of many countries across the continent. In recent years, there has been a concerning resurgence of coups and unconstitutional changes of government \(UCGs\), particularly in the Sahel and West Africa. Nations such as Mali, Burkina Faso, Guinea, Niger, Sudan, and Gabon have all experienced military takeovers, marking a regression in the democratic gains made over the past three decades. These military interventions are frequently fueled and exacerbated by lingering security threats, widespread socio-economic hardship, and severe public dissatisfaction with elected leadership.)
/E (Africa is currently facing serious challenges with political instability and corruption, which continue to deeply affect the socio-economic development and overall peace of many countries across the continent. In recent years, there has been a concerning resurgence of coups and unconstitutional changes of government \(UCGs\), particularly in the Sahel and West Africa. Nations such as Mali, Burkina Faso, Guinea, Niger, Sudan, and Gabon have all experienced military takeovers, marking a regression in the democratic gains made over the past three decades. These military interventions are frequently fueled and exacerbated by lingering security threats, widespread socio-economic hardship, and severe public dissatisfaction with elected leadership.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 100 0 R
/T (Alongside military insurgencies, institutional corruption, weakened judiciaries, disputed electoral processes, and a fundamental lack of official accountability have contributed to a growing crisis of legitimacy and deep-seated distrust between citizens and their governments. Systemic corruption drains critical public resources away from essential infrastructure, healthcare, and education, further exacerbating poverty, youth unemployment, and social inequality. Moreover, the practice of constitutional manipulation including the removal of presidential term limits and the erosion of judicial independence functions as a form of "silent coup" that stifles opposition, limits civic space, and systematically disenfranchises voters.)
/E (Alongside military insurgencies, institutional corruption, weakened judiciaries, disputed electoral processes, and a fundamental lack of official accountability have contributed to a growing crisis of legitimacy and deep-seated distrust between citizens and their governments. Systemic corruption drains critical public resources away from essential infrastructure, healthcare, and education, further exacerbating poverty, youth unemployment, and social inequality. Moreover, the practice of constitutional manipulation including the removal of presidential term limits and the erosion of judicial independence functions as a form of "silent coup" that stifles opposition, limits civic space, and systematically disenfranchises voters.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
