/S /H2
/P 101 0 R
/T (As the African Union, our focus must extend beyond merely managing political crises and imposing sanctions after democratic norms are broken. We must actively confront the underlying structural drivers of instability by strengthening independent electoral commissions, protecting civic space, reinforcing anti-corruption institutions, and guaranteeing civil rights. Restoring citizens faith in democratic governance requires that democracy delivers tangible economic benefits, equitable justice, and genuine political representation. Ensuring long-term continental stability depends on transforming these binding treaties into active, enforceable commitments at national and regional levels.)
/E (As the African Union, our focus must extend beyond merely managing political crises and imposing sanctions after democratic norms are broken. We must actively confront the underlying structural drivers of instability by strengthening independent electoral commissions, protecting civic space, reinforcing anti-corruption institutions, and guaranteeing civil rights. Restoring citizens faith in democratic governance requires that democracy delivers tangible economic benefits, equitable justice, and genuine political representation. Ensuring long-term continental stability depends on transforming these binding treaties into active, enforceable commitments at national and regional levels.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
