/T (Weak institutions cause continental instability. Executive overreach and chronic underfunding degrade judicial bodies and electoral commissions, destroying the rule of law. When administrative irregularities corrupt elections, citizens lose faith in peaceful democratic reform. This legitimacy crisis shrinks civic space, fosters distrust, and creates dangerous political vacuums that invite civil unrest, authoritarian rule, and military takeovers.)
/E (Weak institutions cause continental instability. Executive overreach and chronic underfunding degrade judicial bodies and electoral commissions, destroying the rule of law. When administrative irregularities corrupt elections, citizens lose faith in peaceful democratic reform. This legitimacy crisis shrinks civic space, fosters distrust, and creates dangerous political vacuums that invite civil unrest, authoritarian rule, and military takeovers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
