/S /H3
/P 102 0 R
/T (Vast natural wealth fuels instability through the "resource curse." Heavy reliance on primary commodity exports leaves economies vulnerable to price shocks and inflation. This centralizes wealth, encouraging state capture where elites prioritize capturing resource revenues over funding public services. Consequently, resource concentration breeds corruption, suppresses economic diversification, and drives conflict among factions competing for resource control.)
/E (Vast natural wealth fuels instability through the "resource curse." Heavy reliance on primary commodity exports leaves economies vulnerable to price shocks and inflation. This centralizes wealth, encouraging state capture where elites prioritize capturing resource revenues over funding public services. Consequently, resource concentration breeds corruption, suppresses economic diversification, and drives conflict among factions competing for resource control.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
