/P 102 0 R
/T (Foreign extraction deepens instability through uneven economic exchanges and environmental damage. Foreign entities use unfair contracts to extract raw materials cheaply, keeping high-value processing abroad. Tax evasion and opaque licensing strip host nations of crucial revenue. Furthermore, aggressive extraction causes environmental destruction and local displacement, while foreign backers often support repressive regimes to protect commercial interests.)
/E (Foreign extraction deepens instability through uneven economic exchanges and environmental damage. Foreign entities use unfair contracts to extract raw materials cheaply, keeping high-value processing abroad. Tax evasion and opaque licensing strip host nations of crucial revenue. Furthermore, aggressive extraction causes environmental destruction and local displacement, while foreign backers often support repressive regimes to protect commercial interests.)
/Pg 18 0 R
