/P 107 0 R
/T (Today, Africa stands at a pivotal demographic juncture as its youth cohort rapidly scales toward half a billion individuals. Rather than being absorbed into expanding economic sectors, roughly 10 to 12 million young people enter the continent's labor market each year to compete for fewer than 3 million formal wage jobs. )
/E (Today, Africa stands at a pivotal demographic juncture as its youth cohort rapidly scales toward half a billion individuals. Rather than being absorbed into expanding economic sectors, roughly 10 to 12 million young people enter the continent's labor market each year to compete for fewer than 3 million formal wage jobs. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T (This widening labor deficit means that headline unemployment figures tell only part of the story; nearly 90% of working youth are absorbed into the informal economy, engaged in low-productivity, precarious survival activities with minimal social protections or avenues for upward mobility. )
/E (This widening labor deficit means that headline unemployment figures tell only part of the story; nearly 90% of working youth are absorbed into the informal economy, engaged in low-productivity, precarious survival activities with minimal social protections or avenues for upward mobility. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T (This persistent imbalance severely strains national economies, forcing governments to allocate scarce public revenues toward social safety nets and crisis management rather than foundational infrastructure or innovation. Unlocking this bottleneck remains the central socioeconomic challenge for the continent, as millions of energetic, educated young citizens are sidelined from driving regional productivity. )
/E (This persistent imbalance severely strains national economies, forcing governments to allocate scarce public revenues toward social safety nets and crisis management rather than foundational infrastructure or innovation. Unlocking this bottleneck remains the central socioeconomic challenge for the continent, as millions of energetic, educated young citizens are sidelined from driving regional productivity. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
