/Title (ADDRESSING YOUTH UNEMPLOYMENT AND INNOVATION FOR A STABLE AFRICA)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1169 0 R
/First 1170 0 R
/Last 1170 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 1092 0 R
>>
endobj
1149 0 obj
<<
/Title (In the late 20th century, as newly independent African nations sought to build sovereign economies, many relied heavily on expanding state bureaucracies and public enterprises to absorb the emerging entry-level workforce. However, rapid population growth quickly outstripped government capacity. When structural adjustment programs and economic crises hit the continent in the 1980s and 1990s, governments were forced to implement severe fiscal austerity, freeze public-sector hiring, and privatize state enterprises. This sudden contraction occurred before a robust private sector had taken root to absorb displaced workers, leaving a expanding cohort of young citizens without clear pathways into formal employment.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1092 0 R
/Next 1171 0 R
>>
endobj
1150 0 obj
<<
/Title (Consequently, a severe skill mismatch emerged: millions of young Africans graduated with academic qualifications for industries that no longer had capacity, while high-growth emerging sectors faced acute shortages of locally skilled talent.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1092 0 R
/Prev 1171 0 R
>>
endobj
1151 0 obj
<<
/Title (This widening labor deficit means that headline unemployment figures tell only part of the story; nearly 90% of working youth are absorbed into the informal economy, engaged in low-productivity, precarious survival activities with minimal social protections or avenues for upward mobility.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1000 0 R
/Prev 1093 0 R
/Next 1152 0 R
>>
endobj
1152 0 obj
<<
/Title (This persistent imbalance severely strains national economies, forcing governments to allocate scarce public revenues toward social safety nets and crisis management rather than foundational infrastructure or innovation. Unlocking this bottleneck remains the central socioeconomic challenge for the continent, as millions of energetic, educated young citizens are sidelined from driving regional productivity.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1000 0 R
/Prev 1151 0 R
/Next 1094 0 R
>>
endobj
