/Title (Political instability and corruption are two issues that are often connected. Political instability can take the form of coups, disputed elections, election-related violence, civil conflict, or unconstitutional changes of government. Corruption can include bribery, embezzlement, nepotism, misuse of public funds, and using political power for personal benefit.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1146 0 R
/Next 1180 0 R
>>
endobj
1165 0 obj
<<
/Title (The African Union has recognised the importance of tackling these challenges through initiatives such as agenda 2063 and theAfrican charter on democracy, elections and governance These frameworks focus on building peaceful, democratic, accountable, and well-governed African states. However, it is important to recognise that Africa is not facing one single political situation. Every member state has its own history and challenges, meaning that effective solutions must be realistic, sustainable, and suited to the different circumstances of African countries.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1146 0 R
/Prev 1180 0 R
/First 1181 0 R
/Last 1181 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
1166 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
