/Title (As the late 20th century transitioned into the 21st, this structural job shortage was severely compounded by a widening technological divide. The rapid acceleration of the global digital economy fundamentally altered employer demands, shifting labor requirements toward digital literacy, specialized technical trades, and adaptive problem-solving skills. However, regional education and vocational systems remained largely frozen in colonial-era instructional frameworks that prioritized rote learning and administrative skills over market-aligned technical training.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1092 0 R
/Prev 1149 0 R
/Next 1150 0 R
>>
endobj
