<<
/Title (Vast natural wealth fuels instability through the "resource curse." Heavy reliance on primary commodity exports leaves economies vulnerable to price shocks and inflation. This centralizes wealth, encouraging state capture where elites prioritize capturing resource revenues over funding public services. Consequently, resource concentration breeds corruption, suppresses economic diversification, and drives conflict among factions competing for resource control.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1222 0 R
>>
endobj
1235 0 obj
<<
/Title (Foreign extraction deepens instability through uneven economic exchanges and environmental damage. Foreign entities use unfair contracts to extract raw materials cheaply, keeping high-value processing abroad. Tax evasion and opaque licensing strip host nations of crucial revenue. Furthermore, aggressive extraction causes environmental destruction and local displacement, while foreign backers often support repressive regimes to protect commercial interests.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1223 0 R
>>
endobj
